"Hero-program duels run in System dueling blocks: empty rooms of varied size, e.g. 10 by 25 meters."
"The System announces block, opponent with class and rank, objective, and whether kills are allowed."
"Objectives include incapacitating the opponent or tagging every marked square on their half."
"A timer counts down from five seconds to START; duels may last two minutes."
"Realism can be set to movement restriction only; pain-free realism is usually for the last class."
"Pairings are randomized then adjusted; exhausting one's body or main talent counts as out."
"Attacking after time is called earns laps; injuries are listed and written up afterward."
"The territory game runs 3 minutes on a block about three quarters of a basketball court."
"Squares are tagged with any body part; after the tenth, ten more appear one at a time at random."
"The first to tag 20 squares on the opponent's side wins; injuring is allowed, killing is not."
"Under movement restriction, a simulated broken arm makes the gym suit lock that arm and shoulder."
"The gym's surface is an alien substance that does not count as ground for Shapers."
